title: El contacto
max-visits: 1
view-if: 0
# Container/namespace only. Two forced chains driven by the MAP, not by a die roll:
#   @la_batalla   — a formation has marched onto the column's village. You cannot decline this.
#   @el_cerco     — the same, with every path off the node held. This is the one that ends columns.
# Both are tests of what you have actually accumulated: men, parque, moral, discipline, ground,
# and the water. You never choose whether to fight. You choose how.

# =====================================================================
# LA BATALLA — contact. Three ways out, each with a second decision inside it.
# =====================================================================
@la_batalla
title: Contacto
new-page: true
face-image: img/anti-guerillas.jpg
subtitle: They are here, on this ground, this morning
tags: event
view-if: banda = "sierra" and f_phase = "marcha" and ej_contacto = 1 and cerco_total = 0 and time >= bat_last + 2
priority: 10
frequency: 100
max-visits: 20
on-arrival: {! Q.bat_last=Q.time; Q.bat_plan=""; Q.bat_res="";
// THE GROUND IS A RESOURCE. The deep sierra is worth more than a hundred men.
var _n=Q.col_nodo||"";
var _t = (_n==="elotatal")?26:((_n==="riochiquito")?22:((_n==="elporvenir")?18:((_n==="elquemado")?8:((_n==="sanvicente")?2:-12))));
if((Q.f_campamento===1)&&(Q.camp_nodo===_n)){ _t += 10; }
Q.bat_terreno = _t;
!}

= Contacto

There is no decision about whether this happens. It has already happened: the [? if ej_es_cazador = 1 : cazadores ?][? if ej_es_cazador = 0 : formation ?] that has been walking toward you across the map for weeks is on this ground, this morning, and the column's sentries are firing.

[? if ej_es_cazador = 1 : And these are not the trucks. These are men on foot with rations on their backs and no road behind them, who came up the same vereda you came up, who have been living in this sierra for eleven days waiting to do exactly this. The army has stopped trying to catch you with battalions. It has started sending people who walk. ?][? if ej_es_cazador = 0 : They came up the road, which is the one good thing about them — everything they have is tied to that road, and the road is the shape of what they can do. ?]

[? if bat_terreno >= 18 : The ground is yours. You know every fold of this country and they are reading it off a map drawn from a photograph. ?][? if bat_terreno >= 2 and bat_terreno < 18 : The ground is ordinary — broken enough to fight in, open enough to be caught in. ?][? if bat_terreno < 2 : The ground is bad. This is low country, close to the road, and everything here favours a man with a radio and a mortar. ?]

**La columna:** [+ f_hombres : entero +] fighters · parque [+ f_parque : entero +] · moral [+ f_moral : entero +] · disciplina [+ disciplina : entero +]. **Enfrente:** [? if ej_es_cazador = 1 : los Cazadores ?][? if ej_es_cazador = 0 : la tropa ?], fuerza [+ ej_unidad_f : entero +].

- @bat_romper: **Romper hacia arriba.** Uphill, now, into country their vehicles and their supply cannot follow. *(the classic answer; costs the ground and whatever you drop)*
- @bat_dar: **Dar la cara.** Fight here. Make them pay for coming up, and make every garrison in Guerrero read the report. *(needs men and parque; the biggest result and the biggest bill)*
- @bat_filtrarse: **Filtrarse.** Not a battle and not a retreat — small groups slipping out through their own line in the dark. *(needs discipline; almost bloodless when it works)*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
@bat_romper
new-page: true
face-image: img/sierra_larga.jpg
on-arrival: {! Q.bat_plan="romper"; !}

= Cuesta arriba

The order is four words and the column is moving inside ninety seconds, which is what two years of doing exactly this buys you. Uphill, in file, wounded on the strongest backs, into ground that gets worse for a pursuer with every hundred metres of altitude.

The problem is the tail. Somebody at the back is in contact the whole way, and the whole way there is a question about how much the column is willing to pay to keep the rest of itself intact.

- @bat_r_retaguardia: Leave a rearguard. Six people who hold the draw for an hour so four dozen can get over the ridge. *(you will not get all six back)*
- @bat_r_todos: Nobody stays. Everyone runs, everyone drops what slows them, and the column takes its chances as one body. *(no volunteers left behind; a much messier climb)*

@bat_r_retaguardia
go-to: foco_batalla.bat_fin
on-arrival: {! Q.bat_plan="romper_guardia"; !}

@bat_r_todos
go-to: foco_batalla.bat_fin
on-arrival: {! Q.bat_plan="romper_todos"; !}

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
@bat_dar
new-page: true
face-image: img/guerillas2.jpg
choose-if: f_hombres >= 14 and f_parque >= 12
unavailable-subtitle: Standing and fighting a formation needs at least 14 fighters and 12 parque. You have neither. Move.
on-arrival: {! Q.bat_plan="dar"; Q.f_parque-=12; !}

= Se pelea aquí

You say it out loud so that everyone hears it in the same second, and something goes through the column that is not courage exactly — more like relief. They have been walking away from this for a long time.

Positions in eleven minutes. And then the only question a guerrilla commander ever really answers: do you spread out and survive, or concentrate and win?

- @bat_d_punto: Everything on one point. Mass every rifle against their weakest sector and go through it. *(decisive either way; nothing held in reserve)*
- @bat_d_perimetro: Hold a perimeter and bleed them at range until they lose interest. *(survivable; they will not lose interest quickly)*

@bat_d_punto
go-to: foco_batalla.bat_fin
on-arrival: {! Q.bat_plan="dar_punto"; !}

@bat_d_perimetro
go-to: foco_batalla.bat_fin
on-arrival: {! Q.bat_plan="dar_perimetro"; !}

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
@bat_filtrarse
new-page: true
face-image: img/countrysideravine.jpg
choose-if: disciplina >= 55
unavailable-subtitle: Slipping a whole column through a live enemy line in the dark, in threes, in silence, needs a discipline of 55. This band would be a firefight inside four minutes.
on-arrival: {! Q.bat_plan="filtrarse"; !}

= En la oscuridad

The hardest thing a guerrilla column ever does, and it does not look like anything: forty people going out through a live line in threes, at two in the morning, at a walking pace, in silence, past men who are awake and looking for exactly this.

It works or it does not entirely on whether every single person does the boring thing correctly. One cough. One rifle sling against a rock.

- @bat_f_armas: Bury the heavy weapons and the packs. You can come back for them; you cannot come back for people. *(much quieter; the parque stays in a hole in the sierra)*
- @bat_f_todo: Everything comes out with you. A guerrilla without parque is a hiking club. *(carrying metal past sentries at three metres)*

@bat_f_armas
go-to: foco_batalla.bat_fin
on-arrival: {! Q.bat_plan="filtrarse_ligero"; !}

@bat_f_todo
go-to: foco_batalla.bat_fin
on-arrival: {! Q.bat_plan="filtrarse_pesado"; !}

